# Versions and checksums for binaries Debian does not package.
#
# Copy to config/binaries.env and fill in REAL values. The build fails loudly
# if any required checksum is missing or wrong -- there is deliberately no
# "skip verification" path.
#
# To populate a row:
#   1. Pick a release tag from the project's GitHub releases page.
#   2. Download the asset AND its published checksum file.
#   3. Verify the checksum file's signature where the project publishes one
#      (sops ships cosign attestations; talosctl ships a checksums file).
#   4. Paste the asset URL and its sha256 below.
#
# Record the date you did this in the comment. When you rebuild in two years,
# you will want to know how stale these are.

# --- sops (mozilla/sops -> getsops/sops) ------------------------------------
# Asset naming: sops-vX.Y.Z.linux.amd64  (raw binary, KIND=binary)
#           or: sops_X.Y.Z_amd64.deb     (KIND=deb)
# Checked on: <YYYY-MM-DD>
SOPS_URL=""
SOPS_SHA256=""
SOPS_KIND="binary"

# --- talosctl (siderolabs/talos) --------------------------------------------
# OPTIONAL. Leave TALOSCTL_URL empty to omit talosctl from the image.
# Only needed if the Talos cluster CA / machine secrets are generated on this
# box rather than on a networked workstation.
# Asset naming: talosctl-linux-amd64  (raw binary, KIND=binary)
# Checked on: <YYYY-MM-DD>
TALOSCTL_URL=""
TALOSCTL_SHA256=""
TALOSCTL_KIND="binary"
